Document the StGit overlay workflow and add its helper scripts

Purpose:
Explain and support how this downstream fork keeps its changes (the
Tauri desktop app) as a StGit patch stack on top of upstream
gingko/client master: rebasing onto a newer upstream, sharing the stack
through GitHub so any clone can recover it, and collaborating via topic
stacks and pull requests into the canonical `overlay` stack.

Approach:
- OVERLAY.md: branch/remote layout, update cycle, the "patches are
  intentions" convention (Purpose / Approach / Constraints), sharing,
  collaboration and agent workflows.
- tools/overlay-setup.sh: versioned stand-in for the .git/config that
  git doesn't share (upstream remote, master tracking, stack-ref fetch
  into refs/remote-stacks/origin/*, git aliases, stack restore).
- tools/overlay-publish.sh: atomic push of branch + refs/stacks/<branch>;
  the branch may be forced, the stack ref must fast-forward, which makes
  it the guard against concurrent updates.
- tools/overlay-adopt.sh: make overlay an exact copy of a published
  stack (recovery, landing a reviewed topic), refusing to drop local
  stack work or to adopt a topic cloned from an outdated overlay.
- tools/.gitattributes keeps the scripts LF on core.autocrlf checkouts.

Constraints:
- Touches no upstream file, so it always applies cleanly as the base of
  the stack.
- Never fetch stack refs directly into refs/stacks/*; local stack state
  changes only through stg or overlay-adopt.sh.

